In Classic WoW, most warlocks use Voidwalkers over Succubi for leveling and questing because Voidwalkers provide superior threat generation (Torment, Suffering) and survivability (Sacrifice, Consume Shadows), which are crucial for soloing mobs efficiently. While the Succubus has strong crowd control (Seduction) and stealth (Lesser Invisibility), these are less useful in the context of fast, consistent leveling where threat and self-sustain matter more. Voidwalkers’ abilities better support solo play, making them the preferred choice despite the Succubus’s niche utility. [end of text]


